    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-313371",
      "knowledge_point_id": "261910cd-a1a4-5c90-8caa-238208558458",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Derivative Using the Chain and Quotient Rules",
      "problem": "Given that $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{e}^{2x}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| ${y}^{′}$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $x{e}^{2x}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and the denominator $v(x)={e}^{2x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})({e}^{2x})-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)(2{e}^{2x})}{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{x}-2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{e}^{2x}-2x{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})}{{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}(1-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{x{({e}^{2x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "1-2x\\ln(x)"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "1+2x\\ln(x)"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "1-2x\\ln(x)",
          "choices_complete": false,
